forklift patch 0002 (7a-3, docs/plans/2026-11-26-7a3-sdk-arrival-stamp.md 2): the SDK's sample times from the receive
thread's byte arrival. Applied after 0001 (deploy/ros2/Dockerfile.scan), against Slamtec/sllidar_ros2 34300099.

- The receive thread stamps each read as read() returns (getus, CLOCK_MONOTONIC) and numbers it; the decoder hands
  the codec the bytes with that arrival (IAsyncProtocolCodec::onDecodeDataAt), the codec holds it while it decodes
  them, and the driver gives the unpacker the arrival of the read that completed each sample message
  (forklift::deliverDecoded). The unpacker's clock read returns it -- not the decode time, which waited in the
  receive queue.
- A sample's time is exact only when its unit (capsule, node) ended at the last byte of the codec's block -- the
  unpacker gives a block's last byte to the handler apart; a unit ending inside a block (a resync after a lost byte)
  ended in an earlier read. Capsule handlers keep the exactness with the capsule they cache; the scan holder marks a
  buffer holding any sample that is not exact (or has no arrival at all), and grabScanDataHqWithArrival reports it.
- Every mode stamps a capsule's samples with its own capsule's arrival: Dense and UltraDense took the next capsule's
  time; their capsule, time and exactness now change together (the angle-jump discard included), a reset drops them,
  and enable() resets every handler.
- The unpacker's decode and enable / disable / reset take one lock: a scan restart on the control thread waits for a
  decode in progress, so no capsule cached before it is published after it.
- UltraDense's sample delay used (31 - sampleIdx) for 64 samples a capsule and wrapped to ~2^32 us for the second
  half (an upstream bug); it is (63 - sampleIdx), as UltraBoost's formula is written. The other delays are unchanged.
- The node publishes scan_sdk only in the v2 format: frame_id '<frame>@sdk_mono_v2#<run>.<start>' (run: the
  launcher's forklift_run_id, 8-32 lowercase hex; start: a new random id at every scan start), only for a scan whose
  sample times are all exact arrivals and whose first sample is at least 150 ms after its start (the SDK may hold the
  previous start's samples); each start's mode goes on 'scan_sdk_info' (std_msgs/String JSON: format, run, start,
  ans_type, sample_period_us, baudrate; reliable, transient_local). No run id, no scan_sdk. Scans kept off for an
  inexact time are counted and warned (throttled). The driver is deleted with the node: its threads end before exit.
- FORKLIFT_SDK_RX_LOG=<file> (bench only): each read (R rx_seq rx_us bytes decode_us), each unit that passed its
  checksum (C rx_seq unit_seq ans_type exact), queued and written by a thread of its own; lines that find the queue
  full are counted (D <n>), and 'E <n>' closes a complete record.
- test/forklift_arrival_test.cpp (ctest, BUILD_TESTING): the real transceiver, codec, delivery and handlers on a
  fake channel, reads 80 ms apart, the decoder held 500 ms; a lost byte, a restart during a held callback.

